WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.267
South Korea declaring a

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.169
national period of mourning

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:05.205
after a deadly crowd surge

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:08.441
killed at least 153 people

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:09.342
who were out

00:00:09.342 --> 00:00:10.677
celebrating Halloween

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:12.379
in the capital of Seoul.

00:00:12.379 --> 00:00:13.880
With a warning with some of the images,

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:16.082
we're going to share our graphic.

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:18.018
Authorities are still investigating

00:00:18.018 --> 00:00:18.718
exactly what

00:00:18.718 --> 00:00:20.620
caused this crowd crush,

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:22.489
but emergency officials first began

00:00:22.489 --> 00:00:22.922
receiving

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:24.024
reports of people

00:00:24.024 --> 00:00:27.460
buried in crowds on Saturday evening.

00:00:27.727 --> 00:00:29.863
There were thousands of people out

00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:32.532
that night in an area of the city

00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:34.801
with very narrow streets.

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:37.137
As you can say, they're packed in alleys.

00:00:37.404 --> 00:00:38.238
And witnesses say

00:00:38.238 --> 00:00:40.173
people were trapped and panicked

00:00:40.173 --> 00:00:41.674
because they couldn't breathe.

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:43.176
With dozens of people

00:00:43.176 --> 00:00:46.379
being administered CPR on the sidewalks,

00:00:49.516 --> 00:00:50.483
they turned around

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:52.052
and told the crowd,

00:00:52.052 --> 00:00:54.687
you can't come this way.

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:55.722
People are dying

00:00:58.892 --> 00:00:59.759
Now, police say they

00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:02.028
have confirmed the identities of nearly

00:01:02.028 --> 00:01:04.230
all of those killed as families attempt

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:05.832
to reunite with loved ones

00:01:05.832 --> 00:01:07.634
lost in the chaos.

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:09.202
President Biden

00:01:09.202 --> 00:01:10.570
and the first lady, by the way,

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:11.704
have both offered

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:14.207
their deepest condolences to the families

00:01:14.207 --> 00:01:16.109
of those impacted by this

00:01:16.109 --> 00:01:17.944
horrific tragedy.

00:01:17.944 --> 00:01:19.179
Let's take you to Seoul now

00:01:19.179 --> 00:01:20.480
and CNN's Will Ripley,

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:22.115
who is on the scene shortly

00:01:22.115 --> 00:01:23.583
after this happened.

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:24.784
Will, have officials

00:01:24.784 --> 00:01:26.920
gotten any closer to understanding

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:30.590
exactly how all of this unfolded

00:01:31.091 --> 00:01:31.825
It seems

00:01:31.825 --> 00:01:33.793
as if this may have simply been a case

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:34.961
of so many people

00:01:34.961 --> 00:01:36.096
so excited to be out

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:37.130
for the first Halloween

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:39.032
after COVID restrictions.

00:01:39.032 --> 00:01:40.467
So three years of restrictions

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:42.902
and people were packing into this area.

00:01:42.936 --> 00:01:45.138
We're actually now behind the alleyway

00:01:45.138 --> 00:01:46.940
that we showed you just now on video.

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:47.907
And you can see

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:48.975
this is where a lot of people

00:01:48.975 --> 00:01:50.443
were receiving CPR

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:51.678
you saw lines of bodies

00:01:51.678 --> 00:01:52.679
down in the streets.

00:01:52.679 --> 00:01:53.313
And what's really,

00:01:53.313 --> 00:01:54.614
really striking to me is

00:01:54.614 --> 00:01:56.549
you see that bag there

00:01:56.549 --> 00:01:57.650
with a shoe

00:01:57.650 --> 00:01:58.351
and, you know,

00:01:58.351 --> 00:01:59.953
you see people's Halloween costumes

00:02:01.221 --> 00:02:02.455
I remember seeing

00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:03.289
one of the bodies

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:04.190
that was rolled

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:05.992
by our live position yesterday

00:02:05.992 --> 00:02:07.594
and there was a sheet

00:02:07.594 --> 00:02:08.528
covering the stretcher.

00:02:08.528 --> 00:02:09.929
But you could see

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:12.165
she had a beautiful, glittery princess

00:02:12.165 --> 00:02:13.700
dress on for Halloween.

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:16.102
And anybody who knew her

00:02:16.836 --> 00:02:18.204
would have known that that was her

00:02:18.204 --> 00:02:19.606
just by seeing the costume

00:02:19.606 --> 00:02:21.207
and you think about her

00:02:21.207 --> 00:02:23.576
this young this one woman's parents,

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:26.412
her family, her friends.

00:02:26.412 --> 00:02:28.248
And it's just really heartbreaking.

00:02:28.248 --> 00:02:31.684
97 of those who were killed are women.

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:34.187
56 men out of 153 deaths.

00:02:34.187 --> 00:02:35.722
And they come from

00:02:35.722 --> 00:02:36.789
not just here in South Korea,

00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:37.891
the majority from South Korea,

00:02:37.891 --> 00:02:38.992
but really all over the world.

00:02:38.992 --> 00:02:40.660
I mean, the list up just updated here

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:42.829
Norway, Australia, Japan, Sri Lanka,

00:02:43.096 --> 00:02:45.131
Thailand, Iran,

00:02:45.131 --> 00:02:47.567
all of these people, many of them

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:49.102
in their twenties, in their thirties,

00:02:49.102 --> 00:02:51.237
out here having a great time

00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:52.972
and they never came home.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:54.407
Know

00:02:56.142 --> 00:02:58.545
Halloween horror and heartbreak

00:02:58.945 --> 00:03:01.214
in Seoul's popular nightlife district.

00:03:01.581 --> 00:03:03.316
Nightmare scenes,

00:03:03.316 --> 00:03:05.485
the narrow alleys of each one

00:03:05.485 --> 00:03:07.554
lined with lifeless bodies,

00:03:07.687 --> 00:03:09.489
many in costume

00:03:09.489 --> 00:03:11.124
Frantic first responders

00:03:11.124 --> 00:03:12.559
trying to save them.

00:03:12.559 --> 00:03:15.261
This is a row of stretchers

00:03:15.261 --> 00:03:15.562
that we

00:03:15.562 --> 00:03:16.262
initially thought

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:16.963
were waiting

00:03:16.963 --> 00:03:19.699
for potential survivors of this incident

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:21.601
at a Halloween party

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:22.802
where thousands of people

00:03:22.802 --> 00:03:26.673
were packed into a relatively tight area.

00:03:26.673 --> 00:03:27.907
But in fact, we've now realized

00:03:27.907 --> 00:03:30.276
that these stretchers are being used to

00:03:31.778 --> 00:03:33.646
bring back bodies.

00:03:33.646 --> 00:03:35.815
And we have just seen body after body

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:38.952
rolling pass here that you see

00:03:38.952 --> 00:03:39.986
most of those hurt

00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:41.621
or killed in their late

00:03:41.621 --> 00:03:43.323
teens and twenties.

00:03:43.323 --> 00:03:43.957
The local fire

00:03:43.957 --> 00:03:46.960
chief says young people from South Korea

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:48.361
and beyond.

00:03:48.361 --> 00:03:50.763
Witnesses say Taiwan's iconic

00:03:50.763 --> 00:03:52.098
Halloween festivities

00:03:52.098 --> 00:03:54.567
always draw an international crowd.

00:03:55.134 --> 00:03:56.569
This video on Twitter

00:03:56.569 --> 00:03:59.372
shows an apparent lack of crowd control,

00:03:59.839 --> 00:04:03.243
a sea of bodies pouring into a tiny area.

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:05.044
An ominous warning

00:04:05.044 --> 00:04:06.846
telling people to be careful.

00:04:08.481 --> 00:04:08.982
Police

00:04:08.982 --> 00:04:11.184
and emergency crews rushed to the scene

00:04:11.551 --> 00:04:12.852
shortly after 10 p.m.

00:04:12.852 --> 00:04:14.654
local Saturday night.

00:04:14.654 --> 00:04:16.556
Yonhap News Agency reported

00:04:16.556 --> 00:04:17.590
emergency lines

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:18.858
flooded with calls

00:04:18.858 --> 00:04:20.026
from people in the packed

00:04:20.026 --> 00:04:23.496
area saying they were stuck, suffocating.

00:04:23.997 --> 00:04:25.431
Some who fell down

00:04:25.431 --> 00:04:26.833
apparently crushed

00:04:26.833 --> 00:04:28.901
under a growing pile of people.

00:04:29.402 --> 00:04:31.671
Official causes of death not confirmed,

00:04:31.938 --> 00:04:33.006
but Yonhap reporting

00:04:33.006 --> 00:04:35.341
dozens suffered cardiac arrest.

00:04:35.541 --> 00:04:38.678
And I saw the people's like going to

00:04:39.379 --> 00:04:42.949
the left side and I actually saw

00:04:42.949 --> 00:04:44.817
the person actually get into that

00:04:44.817 --> 00:04:46.219
at the opposite side.

00:04:46.219 --> 00:04:48.621
So actually, the person in the middle,

00:04:48.721 --> 00:04:49.822
they got jammed

00:04:49.822 --> 00:04:51.924
and they they have like, you know,

00:04:51.924 --> 00:04:53.326
no way to communicate.

00:04:53.326 --> 00:04:54.360
And they like you know,

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:55.828
they cannot breathe.

00:04:55.828 --> 00:04:56.195
The fire

00:04:56.195 --> 00:04:58.831
chief calls this a presumed stampede.

00:04:59.132 --> 00:05:01.301
The investigation is ongoing.

00:05:01.301 --> 00:05:02.935
Social media video shows

00:05:02.935 --> 00:05:05.104
emergency crews struggling,

00:05:05.104 --> 00:05:05.638
pulling

00:05:05.638 --> 00:05:07.640
injured and unconscious victims

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:09.609
from the narrow alleyways

00:05:09.609 --> 00:05:11.678
still jammed with hundreds,

00:05:11.678 --> 00:05:14.013
if not thousands of people

00:05:14.013 --> 00:05:16.149
South Korea's president in Tokyo

00:05:16.149 --> 00:05:18.418
holding an emergency cabinet meeting.

00:05:18.418 --> 00:05:19.419
The tragic incident

00:05:19.419 --> 00:05:22.155
now being treated as a national disaster.

00:05:22.622 --> 00:05:25.425
Authorities say hospital beds and morgues

00:05:25.725 --> 00:05:27.293
filling up fast.

00:05:27.293 --> 00:05:28.061
President Yoon

00:05:28.061 --> 00:05:30.563
making rapid identification of victims

00:05:30.563 --> 00:05:31.864
a top priority.

00:05:33.199 --> 00:05:33.800
Anxious

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:35.401
families and friends

00:05:35.401 --> 00:05:37.236
desperately waiting for word,

00:05:37.236 --> 00:05:38.805
waiting for loved ones

00:05:38.805 --> 00:05:41.107
who left for a night of Halloween fun

00:05:41.708 --> 00:05:44.344
and haven't come home

00:05:46.279 --> 00:05:47.647
as of about an hour ago.

00:05:47.647 --> 00:05:48.314
There were

00:05:48.314 --> 00:05:52.185
4100 missing persons cases filed.

00:05:52.452 --> 00:05:54.253
There are about 100,000 people out here.

00:05:54.253 --> 00:05:55.588
Last night, tonight was actually supposed

00:05:55.588 --> 00:05:56.456
to be an even bigger night.

00:05:56.456 --> 00:05:57.357
This is one of the Ali

00:05:57.357 --> 00:05:59.492
the alley, actually, right next door,

00:05:59.492 --> 00:06:00.727
just down the block

00:06:00.727 --> 00:06:02.195
from where this happened.

00:06:02.195 --> 00:06:03.463
This was supposed to be packed tonight.

00:06:03.463 --> 00:06:04.197
And you can see that

00:06:04.197 --> 00:06:05.064
it's completely

00:06:05.064 --> 00:06:06.499
shut down

00:06:06.766 --> 00:06:08.768
this space maybe six and a half

00:06:08.768 --> 00:06:10.403
feet across. Guys.

00:06:10.403 --> 00:06:11.137
Can you imagine

00:06:11.137 --> 00:06:13.206
being stuck in the middle here

00:06:13.206 --> 00:06:16.242
with literally thousands of people

00:06:16.242 --> 00:06:17.977
in this small area

00:06:17.977 --> 00:06:21.180
packing and pushing you

00:06:22.048 --> 00:06:24.917
It's hard to wrap your mind around

00:06:25.351 --> 00:06:26.119
how terrifying

00:06:26.119 --> 00:06:27.153
that must have been for

00:06:27.153 --> 00:06:27.687
those people

00:06:27.687 --> 00:06:29.689
who were essentially crushed to death

00:06:29.689 --> 00:06:31.391
or for those who slipped and fell

00:06:31.391 --> 00:06:33.526
and had people piling up on top of them.

00:06:33.526 --> 00:06:35.128
Some people so desperate,

00:06:35.128 --> 00:06:37.029
you know, they were trying to climb up

00:06:37.029 --> 00:06:37.897
these walls here

00:06:37.897 --> 00:06:38.931
just jumping in

00:06:38.931 --> 00:06:39.932
and grabbing for anything

00:06:39.932 --> 00:06:41.534
they could to get up above

00:06:41.534 --> 00:06:42.402
the crowd of people.

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:44.637
There's a lot of

00:06:44.637 --> 00:06:45.972
questions that need to be answered

00:06:45.972 --> 00:06:46.973
here in South Korea.

00:06:46.973 --> 00:06:48.708
Why were so many people

00:06:48.708 --> 00:06:50.943
allowed to pack into a narrow space

00:06:50.943 --> 00:06:53.146
like this? Where was the crowd control?

00:06:53.746 --> 00:06:54.881
Some of the images

00:06:54.881 --> 00:06:55.815
that we've been showing you,

00:06:55.815 --> 00:06:57.784
they were from an hour, 2 hours

00:06:57.784 --> 00:06:59.552
before this deadly incident.

00:06:59.552 --> 00:06:59.952
Was there

00:06:59.952 --> 00:07:02.855
nobody sounding the alarm saying,

00:07:02.855 --> 00:07:04.290
hey, too many people,

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:05.191
let's clear them out

00:07:05.191 --> 00:07:06.359
before something horrible happens?

00:07:06.359 --> 00:07:06.826
I mean, these are the

00:07:06.826 --> 00:07:07.760
really tough questions

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:09.962
that they're having to ask here.

00:07:09.962 --> 00:07:12.932
But tonight, as you see it's all about,

00:07:12.932 --> 00:07:14.200
well, most people who were here

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:14.667
last night

00:07:14.667 --> 00:07:15.868
want nothing to do with this place.

00:07:15.868 --> 00:07:17.503
Now it's empty.

00:07:17.503 --> 00:07:18.905
Aside from a handful of reporters

00:07:18.905 --> 00:07:21.073
and the police blocking off the area,

00:07:21.073 --> 00:07:22.308
And, of course, those shoes

00:07:23.309 --> 00:07:23.543
and the

00:07:23.543 --> 00:07:25.044
pieces of people's Halloween costumes

00:07:25.044 --> 00:07:27.847
just sitting in trash bags guarantee you

00:07:29.148 --> 00:07:30.316
a lot of the pieces of costumes,

00:07:30.316 --> 00:07:31.083
they're come from people

00:07:31.083 --> 00:07:33.152
who who didn't make it out alive

00:07:33.586 --> 00:07:34.654
yesterday.

00:07:34.921 --> 00:07:36.422
Just heartbreaking details

00:07:36.422 --> 00:07:37.323
to think about,

00:07:37.323 --> 00:07:37.723
you know,

00:07:37.723 --> 00:07:38.558
these costumes

00:07:38.558 --> 00:07:39.592
and how recognizable

00:07:39.592 --> 00:07:41.794
some of the victims may have been Will.

00:07:41.794 --> 00:07:42.161
And John,

00:07:42.161 --> 00:07:43.262
just to give it some context,

00:07:43.262 --> 00:07:43.663
I mean,

00:07:43.663 --> 00:07:46.065
that's an eerie silence that we're seeing

00:07:46.065 --> 00:07:47.400
and not hearing.

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:47.667
Right,

00:07:47.667 --> 00:07:48.668
because each one,

00:07:48.668 --> 00:07:50.002
as some of you may know,

00:07:50.002 --> 00:07:51.938
I've been there before.

00:07:51.938 --> 00:07:54.073
You know, it's a popular entertainment

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:57.176
night district, a place that, you know,

00:07:57.210 --> 00:07:58.945
a lot of foreigners like to frequent.

00:07:58.945 --> 00:08:01.047
It's very popular with U.S.

00:08:01.047 --> 00:08:03.850
soldiers, a big expat community.

00:08:03.850 --> 00:08:07.220
And just just a quick question.

00:08:08.187 --> 00:08:09.755
Were the crowds honest?

00:08:09.755 --> 00:08:10.456
I mean, I guess

00:08:10.456 --> 00:08:12.425
such large crowds unexpected.

00:08:12.425 --> 00:08:13.593
Was there a parade

00:08:13.593 --> 00:08:15.127
or what was exactly supposed to

00:08:15.127 --> 00:08:17.230
take place last night? There?

00:08:18.764 --> 00:08:19.532
Well, there were a lot

00:08:19.532 --> 00:08:20.700
of different parties thrown in,

00:08:20.700 --> 00:08:21.567
I should point out.

00:08:21.567 --> 00:08:23.169
I mean, I've been to Seoul

00:08:23.169 --> 00:08:24.003
dozens of times

00:08:24.003 --> 00:08:25.204
for work covering North Korea,

00:08:25.204 --> 00:08:26.672
just, you know, covering South Korea.

00:08:26.672 --> 00:08:27.306
Over the years.

00:08:27.306 --> 00:08:28.241
It's been a few years

00:08:28.241 --> 00:08:29.842
since I've been here.

00:08:29.842 --> 00:08:32.345
And I can't count how many nights

00:08:32.745 --> 00:08:34.013
I have been along this exact

00:08:34.013 --> 00:08:35.014
same street with friends.

00:08:35.014 --> 00:08:36.048
I celebrated my birthday

00:08:36.048 --> 00:08:38.417
at that restaurant right there.

00:08:38.417 --> 00:08:39.785
This is the place that you go

00:08:39.785 --> 00:08:41.454
if you want to have

00:08:41.454 --> 00:08:44.156
some drinks, have have a meal.

00:08:44.156 --> 00:08:46.058
So this feels

00:08:46.058 --> 00:08:47.226
it feels very personal

00:08:47.226 --> 00:08:48.394
for anybody that has

00:08:48.394 --> 00:08:49.729
that has come to Seoul

00:08:49.729 --> 00:08:50.696
and come to Itaewon,

00:08:50.696 --> 00:08:51.931
which is a very, very popular,

00:08:51.931 --> 00:08:53.699
iconic place, especially on Halloween.

00:08:53.699 --> 00:08:54.600
Halloween is always

00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:56.102
one of their biggest nights

00:08:56.102 --> 00:08:57.136
I think people knew that

00:08:57.136 --> 00:08:58.571
this night was going to be huge.

00:08:58.571 --> 00:08:59.839
I mean, there were live streams.

00:08:59.839 --> 00:09:00.506
People were saying,

00:09:00.506 --> 00:09:02.008
this is going to be the most wild

00:09:02.008 --> 00:09:03.809
Halloween party in Asia, you know,

00:09:03.809 --> 00:09:06.112
because people were so excited

00:09:06.145 --> 00:09:07.113
to just come back out

00:09:07.113 --> 00:09:08.814
and not have to wear a mask on Halloween

00:09:08.814 --> 00:09:09.582
over three years.

00:09:09.582 --> 00:09:11.584
They had to wear a mask on Halloween,

00:09:11.584 --> 00:09:12.618
and they and there were limits on

00:09:12.618 --> 00:09:13.686
crowd size.

00:09:13.686 --> 00:09:15.121
That was not the case this year.

00:09:15.121 --> 00:09:16.222
And so.

00:09:16.422 --> 00:09:18.090
Well, you know, in terms of

00:09:18.090 --> 00:09:18.991
why people died,

00:09:18.991 --> 00:09:19.825
was was the fact

00:09:19.825 --> 00:09:21.360
that alcohol was consumed a factor

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:22.929
in all of these cardiac arrest cases?

00:09:22.929 --> 00:09:24.163
Some doctors are saying that

00:09:24.163 --> 00:09:25.197
that might be the case.

